{
  "source": "Reverted to D:/ASCIIA_BAY/PLAYER/walk-down-cycle.svg's own <g class=\"body|head|armL|armR|legL|legR|shoeL|shoeR\"> structure — the design this session's earlier all-cycles.svg rebake had accidentally replaced with all-cycles.svg's simpler merged-body-groups pattern (matching left/right/up), changing the face and arm animation. This 8-group per-limb structure is the one that shipped before that switch (see walkDown.json.bak) — each group independently translateY-shifted per quarter-step via its own @keyframes, shoeL/shoeR also toggling opacity to tuck a shoe behind the leg mid-stride, composited in the SVG's own paint order (body -> head -> armL -> armR -> legL -> legR -> shoeL -> shoeR). shirtMask/shortsMask are NEW this session (the old .bak predates the mask feature): classified by GROUP membership (only 'body' cells can be shirt/shorts) rather than the row-boundary heuristic all-cycles.svg's merged pattern needed — this source keeps the torso cleanly separate from the near-white shoe highlights and skin-toned limbs, so no row heuristic is needed to avoid leaking either way. Palette: 40-colour k-means++ shared across all 4 frames, matching the original bake's own count. Columns doubled.",
